WEBVTT

00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:05.420
There's something I want to tell all of you.

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:07.990
Yes?

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:13.990
<b>Wholesaler-san</b>

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:12.390
I had oyako-don for dinner last night.

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:12.690
<i>Today, we'll be talking about wholesalers.</i>

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:13.980
<b>Skull-face Bookseller Honda-san</b>

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:16.690
<b>Tell Me! Wholesaler-san</b>

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.810
Wow, that was amazing.

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:21.790
Oh my god, seriously, oh my god!

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:23.500
What did you think, Honda-san?

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:25.540
It was so amazing...

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:27.380
I was about to wet myself.

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:30.170
I'm glad that didn't happen.

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:35.420
<i>This is Wholesaler-san. He's one
 of our business partners.</i>

00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:36.100
<b>Publishing Wholesaler 
a.k.a. Wholesaler-san</b>

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:37.640
<b>The day before...</b>

00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:40.510
Shoot, we're running out of <i>Poe no ****zoku</i>!

00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:43.400
Didn't that just come out the other day?

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:44.600
Only at the storefront?

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:46.180
Didn't we have some in stock?

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:47.290
Nope.

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:50.620
<b>It was around here somewhere</b>

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:49.240
The clan that's out is the only clan we have.

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:50.620
What do you mean by "clan"?

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:55.900
Hey, the database says 
the wholesaler has it in stock.

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:56.260
We have <i>Poe</i>

00:01:56.490 --> 00:01:57.720
I found Wholesaler-san!

00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:59.580
Don't let him get away. 
Keep him in a bear hug.

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:00.360
Yes, ma'am!

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:03.530
<i>Poe no ****zoku</i>? We have none.

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:06.250
But the system says you do.

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:08.020
To be exact...

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:13.640
<b>Agency stock available
 (Didn't say it's in stock)</b>

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:10.640
It's like this.

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:12.790
<i>I don't get it.</i>

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:17.420
<i>Wholesaler-san is essentially 
a wholesaler for books.</i>

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:20.600
We're out!

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:22.840
<i>Some books cause bookstores to fight over them.</i>

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:23.280
<b>Ahh! We're out!</b>

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:23.280
<b>Please!</b>

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:23.280
<b>Please!</b>

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:23.280
Bookstore

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:23.280
<b>* Artist rendition</b>

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:31.290
<b>Honda-san, 
Hello. I've swiped the art books of people
 who look like children from the wholesaler,
 so please make good use of them. 
- Majutsushi, Distribution Division</b>

00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:25.510
<i>"Hello.</i>

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:29.530
<i>I've swiped the art books of people who 
look like children from the wholesaler,</i>

00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:31.290
<i>so please make good use of them."</i>

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:36.750
<i>Some people have such superhuman 
powers, but they are an exception.</i>

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:37.300
Cough 'em up!

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:37.300
<b>Gyah!</b>

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:37.300
<b>Illustration</b>

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:43.940
<b><i>Poe</i> Sold Out</b>

00:02:41.210 --> 00:02:43.940
Meanwhile, it's all sold out!

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:46.860
Fear the 1949 manga artist...

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:48.110
Um....

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:50.450
About <i>Poe</i>...

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:51.910
<b>We'll print more!</b>

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:53.450
Already?!

00:02:53.450 --> 00:02:55.530
So, how many will you be ordering?

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:56.510
Plenty!

00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:58.750
They never send us as many 
as we order, so lots!

00:02:58.910 --> 00:03:00.520
I'm going on my break—

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:03.000
Ah, Wholesaler-san, do you have a moment?

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:05.870
About what we were talking 
about a few days ago...

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:10.410
Section Chief Armor only acts normal
 when she's talking to business partners.

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:13.470
<i>Only</i>, you say?

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:17.440
Shoot, I forgot! There's something
 I absolutely need to ask Wholesaler-san.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:19.550
Why would you forget if you 
"absolutely" need to ask?

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:22.320
Let's schedule it in for tomorrow, then.

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:24.210
Thank you.

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:25.930
Wholesaler-san.

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:26.680
Yes?

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:30.380
<b>We have x copies!</b>

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:30.380
There's a book we haven't been able 
to find even though we've received it.

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:32.140
And it's nowhere to be found?

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:33.110
That's right.

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:36.560
And I don't remember ordering it, either.

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:40.680
<i>A book we received doesn't exist.</i>

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:44.500
<b>Book</b>

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:44.500
<i>These kinds of "What the heck?!"
 incidents are surprisingly common.</i>

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:47.160
Wholesaler

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:47.160
Publisher

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:46.870
<i>The causes being...</i>

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:48.700
We forgot to ship it out!

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:50.680
It was stuck at the warehouse!

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:52.040
Found it!

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:53.850
So you <i>do</i> have it!

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:55.440
What do you mean, you forgot to deliver it?!

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:57.740
Why would it get stuck there?!

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:05.580
<b>It was selling well, so I ordered plenty.
 Please make good use of it ❤ 
- Majutsushi</b>

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:03.550
<i>"It was selling well, so I ordered plenty.</i>

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:05.180
<i>Please make good use of it."</i>

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:09.420
Ah, this is great, but there's nowhere to put it!

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:13.110
<i>I wonder if Assistant Manager Majutsushi 
also ordered that one book we're missing.</i>

00:04:13.110 --> 00:04:16.480
<i>But then he would have left me a note...</i>

00:04:17.330 --> 00:04:19.860
We have x copies!

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:18.370
Found it!

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:19.340
Already?!

00:04:20.030 --> 00:04:23.600
Another floor is holding a niche book fair.

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:27.870
The book you're looking 
for was nominated there.

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:30.070
Oh, I see.

00:04:30.070 --> 00:04:31.350
Honda-san.

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:32.850
You scared me!

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:35.880
Hey, hear me out...

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:39.220
You know that thing you were interested in?

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:41.090
Well, the ticket for it...

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:46.150
Oh man, oh man, I wanna see it again!

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:47.200
I know what you mean.

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:50.970
<i>Come to think of it, she 
chose to sit beside him.</i>

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:50.970
You could watch it over and 
over. It's a masterpiece.

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:55.700
Wholesaler-san, you're quite 
the nerd, aren't you?

00:04:55.700 --> 00:05:01.000
Ah, Section Chief Armor managed
 to expose me, it seems.

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:05.500
I'm happy to get to fit in with 
the retail people, though.

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:07.860
They're making a concept art book!

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:08.760
You think it'll sell?!

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:10.450
It'll sell like mad.

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:12.430
Everyone will want to know 
about the bath scene.

00:05:12.430 --> 00:05:15.020
<i>Now they're talking about work 
with the same excitement.</i>

00:05:15.430 --> 00:05:19.090
Wait, Wholesaler-san, are you...

00:05:19.910 --> 00:05:21.410
A fudanshi?

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:23.460
Haven't I told you?

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:26.700
<i>I suppose it's only natural</i>

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:30.410
<i>that this workplace attracts nice characters.</i>

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:34.970
<b>A Networking Drinking Party for Booksellers</b>

00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:40.790
<i>A lot of our coworkers aren't too enthusiastic
 about joining mixers outside of the company.</i>

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:42.520
I have a manicure appointment today.

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:44.000
Strangers scare me.

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:45.540
I live pretty far away.

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:51.550
<b>S-san</b>

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:47.010
I know what you mean.

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:51.550
The people here tend to be quite independent.

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:55.110
Okay, Honda-san, you'll be the only 
participant in the mixer, correct?

00:05:55.110 --> 00:05:57.210
I guess so. Sorry.

00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:58.690
Not at all.

00:05:58.930 --> 00:06:01.050
<i>This is S-san from Sales 
at another company.</i>

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:01.630
<b>A certain company's Sales
S-san</b>

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:02.800
Let's stir you all up.

00:06:01.390 --> 00:06:10.370
Bookstore

00:06:01.390 --> 00:06:10.370
<b>* Artist rendition</b>

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:03.580
<i>He has a ton of connections,</i>

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:06.700
<i>and likes hosting "borderless" 
drinking parties,</i>

00:06:06.980 --> 00:06:10.040
<i>where he practically stews people from 
bookstores and publishers in a big pot.</i>

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:13.220
Lucky! I'm jealous.

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:15.740
You're so lucky, getting to go 
to a drinking party with S-san!

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:18.980
Are you sure you're going to be all right, 
pretending to be such a social creature?

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:21.520
Honda's not going for social 
reasons, apparently.

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:23.320
It's a deep-dive investigation.

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:28.890
S-san's acquaintances are all 
kind of weird—I mean, unique.

00:06:28.890 --> 00:06:32.170
I thought they might make 
for good material, so...

00:06:32.170 --> 00:06:35.130
Also, I just realized I haven't
 had beer in a while.

00:06:35.130 --> 00:06:36.920
So you're just going to drink!

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:42.600
<b>I don't get it,
too exaggerated</b>

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:42.100
<i>It's about that skull-face bookseller 
who's famous for having skewed content...</i>

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:42.600
<b>Too many foreigners?</b>

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.600
<b>Why is he a skeleton?</b>

00:06:42.820 --> 00:06:44.080
<i>Very well.</i>

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:49.020
<i>Then why don't we try throwing in the 
voices of more actual booksellers?</i>

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:52.000
<i>Although, they're all adults,</i>

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:55.300
<i>so they probably aren't 
going to be </i>that<i> out there.</i>

00:06:56.910 --> 00:07:00.250
I'll say it loud and clear!

00:06:56.910 --> 00:07:02.620
<b>Passionate</b>

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:02.620
Wholesalers don't give two 
shits about bookstores!

00:07:02.620 --> 00:07:05.930
What's the point if you aren't 
going to sell good books?

00:07:05.930 --> 00:07:07.850
I know! So true!

00:07:07.850 --> 00:07:12.760
I told them I want to push it, so I asked for 
100 copies! Know what they sent me?! <i>Three</i>!

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:14.440
That's ten tens not enough!

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:17.070
Yeah! Give us more!

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:19.370
Honda-san, are you all right?

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:20.300
Are you well?

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:22.640
Sorry, I'm overwhelmed.

00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:24.880
This is a huge gathering.

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:28.830
Yeah, there just happened to be a 
lot of people who were free today.

00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:30.650
It's pretty lively in here.

00:07:31.290 --> 00:07:35.610
Oh yeah, we had a fax for a 
mountain of new book orders.

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:37.790
<b>Gotanda's Miura ****ma, 
O-san: bookseller</b>

00:07:35.610 --> 00:07:37.790
I threw them all out.

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:42.550
I'm sorry, we publishers know 
the bookstores have it rough,

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:44.960
<b>Kudanshita's Connection-Hungry Man, 
S-san: Publisher marketing</b>

00:07:42.550 --> 00:07:44.960
but we send out a ton anyway.

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:48.160
No way, O-san, that doesn't cut it!

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:51.090
<b>Homely</b>

00:07:46.230 --> 00:07:51.100
<b>Seijou's Most Considerate,
 K-san: Bookseller</b>

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:50.210
You can't answer all of them in a day.

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:51.100
Right, T-san?

00:07:51.100 --> 00:07:53.600
<b>F Company Sales</b>

00:07:51.100 --> 00:07:53.600
<b>God</b>

00:07:51.430 --> 00:07:53.600
They send dozens a day.

00:07:53.640 --> 00:07:59.510
<b>Ebina's God
T-san: Bookseller</b>

00:07:53.830 --> 00:07:57.870
I respond to faxes the day 
I recieve them. All of them.

00:07:57.870 --> 00:07:59.310
N-No way.

00:07:59.510 --> 00:08:01.200
Can that even be done?

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:03.430
Sure it can. I'm doing it.

00:08:02.740 --> 00:08:07.520
<b>Representing the helpless</b>

00:08:03.430 --> 00:08:05.660
That's new book orders for 
dozens of publishers!

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:07.520
How do you get through all of them yourself?!

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:08.920
Tenacity.

00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:10.320
Tenacity...

00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:15.540
Well, I'm half-joking about the tenacity, 
but you have to respond to the faxes,

00:08:15.540 --> 00:08:17.360
or you won't get your books.

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:19.570
For example, S-san...

00:08:19.570 --> 00:08:20.350
Yes?

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:25.500
Doesn't it impress the publisher if you get 
an immediate response to the faxes you send?

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:26.670
It does.

00:08:26.670 --> 00:08:29.770
It makes me go, "Do it! Ship 
the full order at once!"

00:08:29.770 --> 00:08:33.240
But sometimes, there are books that we 
don't have, even if we want to ship them.

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:34.270
I get it.

00:08:34.270 --> 00:08:36.580
That's why I want to respond right away!

00:08:36.970 --> 00:08:39.170
By leaving an impression,

00:08:39.170 --> 00:08:41.870
I can be sure to have an 
opportunity in the future!

00:08:42.850 --> 00:08:45.310
We're no match for God.

00:08:46.550 --> 00:08:48.870
I don't know if I can reach that level.

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:59.500
What I really care about as a bookseller is 
that people get the books that they want.

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:00.480
Right.

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:04.950
But you know how wholesalers 
send us way less than we order?

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:08.240
Honestly, I'll never forgive them.

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:11.210
<b>Unforgivable</b>

00:09:08.240 --> 00:09:11.210
<i>So unforgivable that he holds a grudge.</i>

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:14.140
Say, you sell comics, right, Honda-san?

00:09:14.140 --> 00:09:15.580
What are you in charge of?

00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:18.800
I handle American comics and big books.

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:20.820
You're like that one...

00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:22.370
<i>Skull-face Bookseller</i>.

00:09:24.390 --> 00:09:26.280
You read it, O-san?!

00:09:26.280 --> 00:09:27.150
Huh? Oh, yeah.

00:09:27.150 --> 00:09:28.320
Wow!

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:30.880
What's it like reading it as a bookseller?!

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:33.870
Dude, wait, no...

00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:37.190
It's disgustingly self-serving.

00:09:37.900 --> 00:09:41.380
I mean, it's not really that 
interesting in real life!

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:43.450
The reality is that it's 
way more work than that!

00:09:43.450 --> 00:09:44.940
All those damn platitudes!

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:48.420
Worst of all, they don't have a single
 complaint about wholesalers!

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:50.880
Well... You're right... Sorry.

00:09:51.350 --> 00:09:54.220
No, why should you apologize, Honda-sa—

00:10:01.690 --> 00:10:05.060
<i>I can sense how he feels!</i>

00:10:06.280 --> 00:10:07.080
Really?

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:07.750
Yes.

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:10.200
Wait, then, er...

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:14.550
Complain more about the wholesalers, dammit!

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:16.910
He's doubling down!

00:10:16.910 --> 00:10:21.330
Well, our wholesaler is super 
nice. He's got lots of fans.

00:10:17.940 --> 00:10:21.290
<i>Do you have a bookstore in your neighborhood?</i>

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:24.050
That's impossible! There's no way 
a wholesaler would be so charming!

00:10:21.940 --> 00:10:28.580
<i>They might be full of passionate, 
delightful people, too.</i>
